  "body": "The way the [rules for identifying an unknown MIME type](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#rules-for-identifying-an-unknown-mime-type) are supposed to work is that _only_ the patterns listed in the table are allowed to be sniffed, including the tag-terminating byte of either space or closing angle bracket. However, both Firefox and Chrome ignore the tag-terminating byte in apparently all instances listed in the table.\r\n\r\nThis is either a security risk in the browsers, or we should update mimesniff to remove the requirement.",
